# LOCAL web pointed at the DEV server's API (https://dev.book-nest.net).
# Usage:  pnpm dev:web:dev          (loads .env.dev via dotenv-cli, runs next dev)
# Copy this file to .env.dev and you're done. .env.dev is gitignored.
# Field docs live in .env.local.example — this file only notes what differs for dev.
#
# Only API_BASE_URL changes. The browser still calls same-origin /api on
# localhost:3000; Next rewrites proxy it server-side to API_BASE_URL, and SSR
# fetches hit it directly. NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL stays localhost because the web
# itself runs locally.
#
# CAVEAT — auth: the dev API issues Secure, dev.book-nest.net-scoped cookies
# that will NOT stick through the localhost proxy, so sign-in may not persist.
# Public / read endpoints (browsing, covers, catalogs) work fine.

NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=
API_BASE_URL=https://dev.book-nest.net
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000
